						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13942398/te-horoi-pai-seeking-greenlight">Te Horoi Pai (Seeking Greenlight)</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4849200">
									

<p>The anomaly leads to the disappearances because the product makes the subjects &quot;visible&quot; (Via smell due to the unique pheromone they secrete) to the aforementioned entities. It is merely implied and I apologize that it isn't straightforwardly stated. Speaking of which, the victims vanish because the entities consume the people that are &quot;marked&quot; by the pheromone.</p>
<p>The concept isn't very straight forward, but I acknowledge that I see it as a hook as it means the readers would have to pay attention to the details in the article to answer any remaining questions (E.G: The fate of the victims as you asked before, it would be data expunged initially but the testing logs will reveal that the people are consumed).</p>
<p>The discordance appears as such, as I imagined that a G.O.I that did manufacture this anomalous product were either ignorant of, or perhaps aware of the anomalous properties. For the former, I do consider perhaps extending the appearance of symptoms to a few days or weeks, whilst also proving to be more challenging for the Foundation to contain (As people could be able to &quot;spread&quot; the anomaly more, before getting consumed by the entities).</p>
<p>The representation of subconscious fetishes or extremest fears is, the way I imagined it, the byharmless product of manner that these extradimensional entities will manifest in the SCP Foundation's universe. Residing in a parallel dimension with similar yet different constants to our own, they are typically blind and hunt through scent. The entities feed on a herb or plant native to their dimension that produce the anomalous pheromone.</p>
<p>With that in mind, perhaps a G.O.I managed to &quot;tap&quot; into their resident dimension and found a means to extract the ointment through a ritual or some form of dimensional travel to acquire such a pheromone. In the case of a secondary anomalous object that permits travel to the native dimension of the SCP, it could open up the possibility of revealing the pheromone's true origin through an exploration log.</p>
<p>Fetish is used in a very neutral context, being used as an umbrella term for any kind of obsession a person may have, if that is too demonizing then I will find an alternate way to describe it. It is not being likened to extreme fear either, I will make it more clear in the article that the appearance they take is mutually exclusive (50% chance they appear as a person's fetish (The subjects are zealous at this stage, so their insanity will lead them to fall for the passive lure OR a 50% chance that they appear in more aggressive and hostile form e.g: an extreme fear).</p>
<p>I hope that this answers a few of your questions.</p>

							</div>

								
					
