<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A sentient stethoscope capable of speech, with extensive knowledge of non-anomalous medical ailments, and human anatomy. The anomaly can accurately diagnose patients by sight alone, even if the affliction isn’t currently visible When an individual attempts to take any prescription medication that they are not currently prescribed, they will be compelled not to the first time, and the stethoscope will angrily inform them about the dangers of taking unprescribed medicine, and warn them not to. If the individual decides to take it anyway, they will gain a severe and often outlandish form of whatever ailment the medication treats. If they choose not to, a non-anomalous lollipop will materialize near the subject.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The item is recovered from an otherwise normal hospital after reports from a nurse who attempted to abuse opiates while hiding in a storage closet. During recovery, the anomaly cries out in protest and then refuses to communicate until a researcher threatens to take Adderal during an interview. After learning they are conversing with a doctor, the anomaly opens up, detailing its creation. The item promises full cooperation so long as they are allowed to practice medicine or be in the vicinity of a clinic, as that is their sole purpose for existence. After being asked if they have ever signed a Hippocratic Oath, the item replies that they find it nonsensical, and instead signed an Oath of their own design, that allows them to punish patients for “failure to follow basic instructions or general stupidity,” among other things. A selection from the oath is engraved into the side of the anomaly, and a full paper copy is retrieved from the location the anomaly states it was created in. Several tests follow, wherein the item diagnoses several subjects with near-perfect success, and punishes subjects with effects that reciprocate the medications they take. After being presented with an individual afflicted by another SCP, the item expresses confusion, and is unable to diagnose, or offer any treatment. After proving itself, the item is transferred to Site 20 to aid in medical duties.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The secondary anomalous effects are dark, with a small hint of humor. I thought it’d be neat.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> None</p>

